fn sec_cost io -> io
x12002 call open p0 13
x12003 write x12002 4
x12004 write x12003 1
x12005 text "cost"
x12006 puts x12004 x12005
x12007 call open x12006 11
x12008 write x12007 2
x12009 text "Cost"
x12010 puts x12008 x12009
x12011 call close x12010 
x12012 call open x12011 2
x12013 write x12012 4
x12014 write x12013 2
x12015 text "q"
x12016 puts x12014 x12015
x12017 write x12016 2
x12018 text "What does a whole edit cost a model, counting the instructions, the code it reads and its reply?"
x12019 puts x12017 x12018
x12020 call close x12019 
x12021 call open x12020 2
x12022 write x12021 4
x12023 write x12022 2
x12024 text "take"
x12025 puts x12023 x12024
x12026 write x12025 2
x12027 text "At 4000 functions an A0 edit costs 706 tokens against 143854 for TypeScript, which is 203.8x fewer than TypeScript shown the whole numbered file (A0's scoped view against a whole-file workflow, not both with scoped views). At 1 function A0 costs 2.42x TypeScript's tokens and 2.29x Rust's. Sonnet, cache-adjusted."
x12028 puts x12026 x12027
x12029 call close x12028 
x12030 call open x12029 2
x12031 write x12030 2
x12032 text "Cost here is every token a model reads and writes to make one edit: the instructions it is first given (the primer), the code it reads, and its reply. A model edits one function through a scoped view: the function, the signatures it depends on, and its callers. The view stays the same size as the program grows; a numbered whole file does not, so against a whole-file workflow A0's advantage grows with program size and reverses on a one-function file, where the primer dominates."
x12033 puts x12031 x12032
x12034 call close x12033 
x12035 call open x12034 2
x12036 write x12035 2
x12037 text "That is an advantage of the workflow, not of the language. When TypeScript, Rust, Python, Go, Java, C and Ruby are given an equal view (a parse-derived function and its callees, numbered line edits), pooled over the four program sizes (96 trials per cell) A0 canonical costs 318 tokens for one cold task and 176 in an unbounded session, against 386 and 138 for TypeScript and 375 and 115 for Ruby, so it is cheaper cold and dearer once the primer is cached; A0 dense costs 273 and 99. results/ai-edit-scoped.json."
x12038 puts x12036 x12037
x12039 call close x12038 
ret x12039
end

